      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T13:44:16Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): Pass start plans each nested material part from its own edges\n\nThe third read of PR #3353 (head 9939a6238) found material inside a\nhole left standing: the Outside fill read nested outer loops as holes,\nso the bore of a hollow boss or the stock inside a ring part got one\nring along its edge and its middle stayed uncut, with no warning.\n\nEach part of the material (an outer loop with its own holes) is now\nplanned from its own edges; Inside on a part with no hole cuts it core\nfirst, as Auto, with a note. A completeness guard sweeps the passes of\neach start-side plan: if more than 0.1 mm2 of the cutter-centre area\nstays unswept, the level takes the Auto plan with a named \"Pass start\"\nwarning. More clip tests (a vertex on the boundary, a tangent touch, an\nedge overlap); non_sliver_center moves to pocket_plan.rs.\n\nRefs #3316\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
