      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T17:54:32Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): the offset pass-start fallback warns\n\nThe completeness guard's fallback note (\"Pass start <side>: the rings\nfrom the start side would leave A mm2 of this area uncut ...\") did not\ncarry RINGS_FALLBACK, so rings_fallbacks() counted zero and a 2D Offset\nposted no StrategyFallback warning when the guard fell back to the Auto\norder. Route the note through RINGS_FALLBACK, so the op posts one\nadvisory Warning::StrategyFallback (#3035) plus the \"Pass start\" note,\nas the rest of the pass-start family does.\n\nPins: motion linux `the_guard_fallback_is_an_offset_rings_fallback` and\napp `the_offset_guard_fallback_is_a_strategy_fallback`; the Inside fig8\npin also asserts that a complete band posts no fallback warning.\n\nRefs #3316\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "eabff766e7ed55469c451c1029a641eff98ee0bd",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/eabff766e7ed55469c451c1029a641eff98ee0bd"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/commits/3c3f13eb4f8a1d24717b3dce9fb4addd6c38eec9",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": false,
